1
00:00:14,664 --> 00:00:26,574
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,542 --> 00:02:07,932
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:15,242
You proposed me Bannerlordship in
return of my life.

4
00:02:16,854 --> 00:02:20,854
And I propose you an honorable death,
Balgay.

5
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:35,110
Commander Balgay. How did Osman know
we would be coming here?

6
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:39,260
I will figure that out before I cut his
tongue, Kongar.

7
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:46,997
Just as you scared so many people, try to
scare me with your sword now!

8
00:02:48,686 --> 00:02:52,506
I am going to rip your heart, Osman!

9
00:02:54,383 --> 00:02:55,263
Soldiers!

10
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:57,810
Prepare to die!

11
00:02:58,403 --> 00:02:59,663
For Elhan!

12
00:02:59,793 --> 00:03:02,123
Elhan, hear us roar!

13
00:03:02,593 --> 00:03:05,073
Elhan, hear us roar!

14
00:03:07,936 --> 00:03:09,646
With the help of Allah!

15
00:03:18,388 --> 00:03:21,588
My mother and father will finally find
peace today, Kongar!

16
00:03:26,734 --> 00:03:28,994
Let our armors be hard, let our sword
be sharp.

17
00:03:29,934 --> 00:03:32,034
And let your head fall onto ground.

18
00:04:09,571 --> 00:04:12,911
Ambush huh? You forgot the spite of
Mongols very fast, Samsa.

19
00:04:12,981 --> 00:04:15,211
Balgay will also make you pay for this.

20
00:04:15,624 --> 00:04:19,624
It’s time for Balgay to save himself from
Osman Bey’s claws right now.

21
00:04:19,624 --> 00:04:22,043
You better mind your own business,
Cerkutay!

22
00:04:34,957 --> 00:04:37,147
You Cerkutay, you!

23
00:04:59,129 --> 00:05:00,099
Cetinalp!

24
00:05:03,534 --> 00:05:05,014
Take two Alps with you!

25
00:05:05,014 --> 00:05:07,314
And follow this dog wherever he goes...

26
00:05:07,942 --> 00:05:09,402
…and kill him.

27
00:05:09,402 --> 00:05:10,382
Go now!

28
00:05:11,348 --> 00:05:13,948
Cerkutay must have had more of his dogs
on his side…

29
00:05:14,419 --> 00:05:16,519
…it’s obvious his dogs are with Balgay
now.

30
00:05:17,593 --> 00:05:20,323
We need to help Osman Bey as soon as
possible. Let’s go!

31
00:05:28,433 --> 00:05:31,713
If I die before I make Kayis go extinct…

32
00:05:31,713 --> 00:05:33,745
…let me burn in Eylikhan’s hell!

33
00:05:34,425 --> 00:05:36,025
I will be your own hell.

34
00:06:13,919 --> 00:06:14,939
Osman!

35
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,780
I came here to take your life, Osman!

36
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:22,890
To take your life!

37
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:26,560
Uncle?

38
00:06:41,451 --> 00:06:43,621
Your death has arrived, Osman.

39
00:06:54,579 --> 00:06:55,729
What's the matter?

40
00:06:56,209 --> 00:06:57,529
Your half-father is here.

41
00:06:57,529 --> 00:06:59,299
Aren’t you happy, Osman?

42
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:07,307
You killed my son, my Batur. Osman!

43
00:07:12,343 --> 00:07:16,343
You shed the blood of your own kin in
Tent of Suleiman Sheikh!

44
00:07:21,141 --> 00:07:23,031
Drown in your own blood!

45
00:07:23,031 --> 00:07:23,751
Die!

46
00:08:25,765 --> 00:08:29,265
What would you tell me if you had seen my
condition right now, son?

47
00:08:29,783 --> 00:08:35,073
My arms and wings are broken while there
is a constant fire burning inside me.

48
00:08:37,405 --> 00:08:42,765
Would say stay strong mother if you
had seen me right now?

49
00:08:45,448 --> 00:08:49,348
How can I stay strong in a situation
like this, my child?

50
00:08:51,001 --> 00:08:53,251
I wish you had not try to find Gunduz.

51
00:08:54,717 --> 00:08:56,447
I wish my tongue had fallen off.

52
00:08:58,446 --> 00:09:00,766
It was all for protecting, my little one.

53
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,361
Or else, how could I sacrifice you?

54
00:09:05,542 --> 00:09:09,072
I only meant to protect and watch over.

55
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:13,190
My heart is on fire, my son.

56
00:09:45,147 --> 00:09:47,337
I just can’t make head or tail of it.

57
00:09:48,249 --> 00:09:51,039
Why would Osman kill my Batur brother?

58
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:53,500
There is neither proof nor witness.

59
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:54,370
Aygul!

60
00:09:55,898 --> 00:09:57,458
Don’t you know Osman?

61
00:09:59,111 --> 00:10:01,041
He killed your brother.

62
00:10:04,849 --> 00:10:07,159
Are you still in love with him?

63
00:10:09,219 --> 00:10:10,119
Huh?

64
00:10:11,701 --> 00:10:14,341
If so, I hope your heart rots, Aygul!

65
00:10:14,681 --> 00:10:16,531
Let your heart rot!

66
00:10:19,981 --> 00:10:21,841
He was the same.

67
00:10:22,028 --> 00:10:24,498
Osman was the same when he was growing up.

68
00:10:25,463 --> 00:10:27,883
He would just do whatever he wanted to do.

69
00:10:28,633 --> 00:10:31,453
Neither his father nor my Dundar managed
to restrain him.

70
00:10:32,854 --> 00:10:38,014
I have been constantly telling he would
bring our end but nobody listened to me.

71
00:10:38,964 --> 00:10:41,434
Whatever happened only happened to my son.

72
00:10:42,535 --> 00:10:43,445
Bamsi.

73
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,155
Abdurrahman.

74
00:10:45,155 --> 00:10:46,179
Gunduz.

75
00:10:46,725 --> 00:10:47,725
Selcan.

76
00:10:48,686 --> 00:10:50,646
All supported him.

77
00:10:53,803 --> 00:10:56,063
They did not let anybody say anything.

78
00:10:56,063 --> 00:10:58,613
They did not let any dust fall upon his
character.

79
00:10:58,946 --> 00:11:01,276
At the end, they all made my son lose his
life.

80
00:11:02,397 --> 00:11:04,727
However, they always protected Osman.

81
00:11:07,451 --> 00:11:09,631
Do I have your permission, Zohre Hatun?

82
00:11:09,695 --> 00:11:10,495
Come in.

83
00:11:16,283 --> 00:11:19,663
Selcan and Gonca Hatun have just had their
horses be ready.

84
00:11:19,663 --> 00:11:20,773
They are leaving the Tent.

85
00:11:20,773 --> 00:11:21,633
Is that so?

86
00:11:23,636 --> 00:11:25,756
Wow, Selcan Hatun. Wow!

87
00:11:29,770 --> 00:11:31,610
Untill your blood spills...

88
00:11:33,081 --> 00:11:35,961
…let burying my son be illicit for me.

89
00:11:35,961 --> 00:11:36,721
Mother!

90
00:11:36,995 --> 00:11:38,755
I beg you please act yourself!

91
00:11:38,859 --> 00:11:40,249
Don’t speak!

92
00:11:40,249 --> 00:11:41,479
Go arm yourself!

93
00:11:42,657 --> 00:11:46,657
They killed my Batur, of course they will
drown in their own blood.

94
00:11:47,209 --> 00:11:48,029
Get up!

95
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:53,850
That parasite will pay for my son’s life!

96
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:56,810
I’ll revenge my Batur's blood...

97
00:11:57,673 --> 00:11:59,773
...with his own sword.

98
00:12:00,817 --> 00:12:01,557
Mother!

99
00:12:02,405 --> 00:12:04,785
Selcan Hatun has Alps.

100
00:12:05,710 --> 00:12:07,390
What do you think we can do?

101
00:12:08,054 --> 00:12:09,754
Please don’t do it.

102
00:12:10,006 --> 00:12:11,746
Don’t we have our own Alps?

103
00:12:13,026 --> 00:12:15,106
Go and let the Alps know.

104
00:12:15,115 --> 00:12:16,195
Prepare the horses.

105
00:12:16,435 --> 00:12:17,735
We will follow them.

106
00:12:21,356 --> 00:12:22,286
Mother!

107
00:12:23,042 --> 00:12:24,582
I told you to arm yourself!

108
00:12:25,615 --> 00:12:28,225
I can not rest until that woman spits
blood.

109
00:12:28,897 --> 00:12:29,747
Go now!

110
00:12:56,724 --> 00:12:57,954
Samsa!

111
00:12:59,685 --> 00:13:00,925
Come on Valiants!

112
00:13:01,463 --> 00:13:03,623
Kill them all and don’t spare their lives!

113
00:13:03,892 --> 00:13:06,132
Be with us Allah!

114
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:30,140
You will die, Osman!

115
00:14:33,437 --> 00:14:34,687
You got away again!

116
00:14:44,719 --> 00:14:45,589
Osman!

117
00:14:47,142 --> 00:14:50,142
Drown in your blood, Osman!

118
00:14:52,138 --> 00:14:53,258
Osman.

119
00:14:55,873 --> 00:15:00,473
Genghis Khan says who he fights knowing
he will lose is a fool.

120
00:15:00,907 --> 00:15:01,647
Come!

121
00:15:10,688 --> 00:15:11,678
Konur!

122
00:15:11,871 --> 00:15:13,171
Follow Balgay!

123
00:15:13,467 --> 00:15:15,227
Dear or alive, I want both of them.

124
00:15:15,227 --> 00:15:16,137
Go!

125
00:15:47,064 --> 00:15:47,824
Uncle.

126
00:15:48,245 --> 00:15:49,015
Uncle!

127
00:15:55,922 --> 00:15:56,952
Dundar Bey!

128
00:16:16,627 --> 00:16:17,487
Osman...

129
00:16:18,319 --> 00:16:21,679
...I will be the one who brings your end.

130
00:16:22,279 --> 00:16:24,689
Yet, Dundar Bey is dead.

131
00:16:25,752 --> 00:16:27,222
He should not die, Melik.

132
00:16:27,222 --> 00:16:28,502
He should not!

133
00:16:28,502 --> 00:16:29,912
I need Dundar.

134
00:16:30,462 --> 00:16:32,662
We must make sure!

135
00:16:33,231 --> 00:16:36,031
Osman!

136
00:16:37,167 --> 00:16:41,467
I will rip you with my own hands when
the time comes.

137
00:17:01,147 --> 00:17:05,527
If Zohre Hatun learns that we left
the Tent, she will follow us.

138
00:17:07,145 --> 00:17:09,265
We are close to Kurgan Valley.

139
00:17:09,825 --> 00:17:11,954
If she's coming, she will see.

140
00:17:13,875 --> 00:17:17,385
Come on, there is no rest for the weary.

141
00:17:46,019 --> 00:17:47,809
They are going towards Kurgan Valley.

142
00:17:48,269 --> 00:17:49,659
We will ambush them.

143
00:17:51,681 --> 00:17:53,511
Mother, please don’t.

144
00:17:53,983 --> 00:17:55,183
Let’s head back.

145
00:17:55,497 --> 00:17:58,127
We left my brother in the Tent.
Please don’t.

146
00:17:58,512 --> 00:17:59,642
You go back.

147
00:18:00,812 --> 00:18:03,252
I will be seeking the revenge of my son.

148
00:18:04,011 --> 00:18:06,111
I won’t come back until I kill them.

149
00:18:07,648 --> 00:18:10,328
Now, listen to me carefully.

150
00:18:11,733 --> 00:18:14,643
From now on, we will continue our road
with our swords.

151
00:18:16,013 --> 00:18:23,533
Selcan Hatun is one of the stooges of
your Batur Bey’s, my son’s killer.

152
00:18:26,503 --> 00:18:29,073
Today is the day for revenge.

153
00:18:29,938 --> 00:18:32,598
There is no going back before we cut their
breaths.

154
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:34,050
Let’s go!

155
00:19:02,239 --> 00:19:04,429
They are following us, Commander Balgay.

156
00:19:04,429 --> 00:19:06,859
You are wounded, we need to lose our
track.

157
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:11,798
Warm water will make us lose our track…

158
00:19:11,798 --> 00:19:13,318
…but not our hatred.

159
00:19:40,906 --> 00:19:43,296
They used this water to lose their track.

160
00:19:44,076 --> 00:19:46,816
We can’t go back unless we find them.

161
00:19:46,816 --> 00:19:48,626
We need to keep searching for them.

162
00:19:48,892 --> 00:19:52,272
My brother, you will leave them to me once
we find them.

163
00:19:52,883 --> 00:19:53,873
For what?

164
00:19:54,257 --> 00:19:56,847
Do you think I will go crazy and comply
with him again?

165
00:19:56,847 --> 00:19:59,563
I know this time he will not bother
to kill, my Kongar.

166
00:19:59,563 --> 00:20:02,233
And I don’t want you to go into brother
massacre.

167
00:20:02,233 --> 00:20:04,073
He is not my brother.

168
00:20:04,073 --> 00:20:09,683
His blood is helal since they stabbed my
father in the back and ravaged our Tent.

169
00:20:41,022 --> 00:20:42,102
Speak now.

170
00:20:50,654 --> 00:20:51,454
Speak.

171
00:20:52,517 --> 00:20:54,177
What happened to Batur?

172
00:20:54,177 --> 00:20:55,017
Huh?

173
00:20:55,017 --> 00:20:56,827
What happened to Batur?

174
00:21:01,179 --> 00:21:03,699
You ask as if you don’t know already.

175
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:07,990
You killed Batur and sent his body
to Tent with a horse.

176
00:21:08,084 --> 00:21:10,144
What else are you asking?

177
00:21:10,443 --> 00:21:12,833
My Osman, what is he saying?

178
00:21:13,414 --> 00:21:15,554
I don’t understand.

179
00:21:19,648 --> 00:21:23,622
I don’t understand, Bamsi Bey, but
we will, eventually.

180
00:21:23,622 --> 00:21:28,524
What important right now is Dundar Bey. He
is alive and what he tells us matters.

181
00:21:28,524 --> 00:21:31,374
So, he still has a lot to suffer.

182
00:21:32,444 --> 00:21:35,524
His soldiers are alive also.

183
00:21:36,852 --> 00:21:40,222
Abdurrahman Ghazi, take Erkut and Kılıç
with you.

184
00:21:41,226 --> 00:21:45,726
And take Dündar
Bey along with these two to Elif Mother.

185
00:21:46,046 --> 00:21:48,610
The cave is close to Hawk Rocks.

186
00:21:48,610 --> 00:21:51,450
- We will be there within a short time.
- But...

187
00:21:52,314 --> 00:21:55,344
My uncle has to live. You
understand it, right?

188
00:21:55,764 --> 00:21:58,194
Don’t you worry, my Osman.

189
00:22:00,037 --> 00:22:03,857
The dog who killed Batur and set Dündar
Bey against us is the same person.

190
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:08,660
We can only learn whichever
dog it is from Dundar Bey.

191
00:22:10,883 --> 00:22:14,253
- Come on, build a sledge!
- As you wish, my Bey.

192
00:22:16,713 --> 00:22:20,393
Now, come here!

193
00:22:21,071 --> 00:22:24,191
Who told you that we were here?

194
00:22:26,941 --> 00:22:28,681
Who?

195
00:22:31,893 --> 00:22:33,593
Speak!

196
00:22:33,765 --> 00:22:35,775
Speak!

197
00:22:36,032 --> 00:22:40,022
Somebody you haven’t seen before.

198
00:22:51,076 --> 00:22:54,968
- Who sent you?
- Balgay sent me, Dündar Bey.

199
00:22:54,968 --> 00:22:59,038
- What does he want?
- Balgay knows where Osman is.

200
00:22:59,038 --> 00:23:02,748
He is at Uhud Hills and
asks for your presence.

201
00:23:31,996 --> 00:23:36,776
It is not Balgay who sent Dündar
Bey, huh my Osman?

202
00:23:38,342 --> 00:23:42,152
Then who made Dundar Bey follow Balgay?

203
00:23:42,169 --> 00:23:45,469
The one who shot Dundar Bey
with that arrow, Samsa Bey.

204
00:23:46,848 --> 00:23:54,448
It is obvious somebody is trying all he
can to make me and my uncle enemies.

205
00:23:56,373 --> 00:23:58,933
It’s neither Balgay...

206
00:23:59,638 --> 00:24:01,818
...nor Yannis.

207
00:24:03,151 --> 00:24:06,491
Sooner or later, we will
find who that traitor is.

208
00:24:08,075 --> 00:24:12,365
But how are we going to do that, my Osman?

209
00:24:12,669 --> 00:24:17,629
We will go to Tent and take
my father’s consignations.

210
00:24:18,832 --> 00:24:22,832
Until today, Kayı
Tent has never been without a ruler.

211
00:24:23,293 --> 00:24:26,513
And from now, it will not ever again.

212
00:24:26,868 --> 00:24:30,047
We will not stop until we make
the ones who stepped on...

213
00:24:30,047 --> 00:24:35,097
our customs and betrayed us
pay for what they did.

214
00:24:35,332 --> 00:24:37,513
Praise be, my lion.

215
00:24:37,513 --> 00:24:45,283
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

216
00:24:58,365 --> 00:25:02,405
Come on. We
shouldn't be afraid, Gonca.

217
00:25:02,425 --> 00:25:07,049
I worry about you, Selcan Hatun. I have to
protect you.

218
00:25:08,579 --> 00:25:15,195
I am an old girl, I always
take precautions.

219
00:25:15,195 --> 00:25:18,185
Don't worry. Come on.

220
00:26:25,739 --> 00:26:28,549
I swear that...

221
00:26:28,783 --> 00:26:33,053
Kayıs' blood will flow like this stream.

222
00:26:34,783 --> 00:26:37,393
I swear on the flying bird...

223
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:41,700
Kayıs' leader will fly like this.

224
00:26:42,451 --> 00:26:45,681
I swear on the land...

225
00:26:45,928 --> 00:26:49,788
the land will be full of dead people.

226
00:26:55,580 --> 00:26:58,930
How could Osman set a
trap, Commander Balgay?

227
00:27:03,199 --> 00:27:09,789
Don't you get it? They set me
a trap with Yannis.

228
00:27:11,743 --> 00:27:17,963
Sneaky like a snake,
crafty like a fox.

229
00:27:18,675 --> 00:27:24,665
A novice boy and an old
imbecile set me a trap.

230
00:27:25,466 --> 00:27:28,434
You promised Yannis more than he deserved.

231
00:27:28,434 --> 00:27:31,584
Why did Yannis betray you?

232
00:27:33,258 --> 00:27:40,418
My promises were killed
by Osman's weapon, Kongar.

233
00:27:40,767 --> 00:27:45,457
Let's find a cave and take shelter.

234
00:27:46,964 --> 00:27:50,174
We should gain power.

235
00:27:50,332 --> 00:27:55,032
Osman will understand that
Balgay isn't defeated.

236
00:28:45,434 --> 00:28:48,254
Did you find Sofia?

237
00:28:48,393 --> 00:28:50,753
We're still looking, sir.

238
00:28:50,776 --> 00:28:55,516
If you can't find Sofia, you know
what's going to happen to you.

239
00:28:55,934 --> 00:28:58,284
Yes, sir. I know.

240
00:28:58,284 --> 00:29:04,164
No, you can't even imagine
what I'll do to you.

241
00:29:05,108 --> 00:29:10,069
Sir, we looked at everywhere. It's like...

242
00:29:10,069 --> 00:29:11,789
Shut up!

243
00:29:15,469 --> 00:29:17,419
Did Osman...

244
00:29:17,629 --> 00:29:20,409
kill Balgay?

245
00:29:20,946 --> 00:29:25,096
There are many dead Mongols in Uhud
Hills and İnegöl borders.

246
00:29:25,704 --> 00:29:28,864
But Balgay isn't one of them.

247
00:29:28,864 --> 00:29:34,684
If Osman fails to keep Balgay, Mongols
will make us pay for it.

248
00:29:34,918 --> 00:29:37,708
We've been played by Osman.

249
00:29:39,784 --> 00:29:45,694
This trap will be our death, I'm afraid.

250
00:30:56,168 --> 00:30:59,558
- Protect yourself!
- Zöhre Hatun!

251
00:31:18,765 --> 00:31:21,215
What is it, Zöhre?

252
00:31:21,253 --> 00:31:25,733
Are you a bandit now? Or a looter?

253
00:31:52,826 --> 00:31:55,936
Osman killed my son.

254
00:31:56,298 --> 00:31:59,008
And you helped him.

255
00:31:59,304 --> 00:32:01,934
You'll pay for it, Hatun!

256
00:32:01,983 --> 00:32:06,143
Batur died because of your evilness.

257
00:32:09,043 --> 00:32:17,343
I thought you were smart. But, are you
being like your mother now?

258
00:32:17,416 --> 00:32:21,076
I belong to my mother's side.

259
00:32:22,829 --> 00:32:26,349
Do you think I won't take my
brother's revenge?

260
00:32:29,763 --> 00:32:35,695
I understand. They want blood.

261
00:32:35,695 --> 00:32:39,675
I'll kill you, Selcan Hatun.

262
00:32:42,612 --> 00:32:45,322
Drop your weapon, Selcan Hatun.

263
00:32:46,220 --> 00:32:52,250
Come on, let's hope that your
Osman will save you.

264
00:33:12,206 --> 00:33:17,116
We hoped for one, but Allah gave us two.

265
00:33:21,258 --> 00:33:25,298
The ones who we wish to be dead
are facing us, mother!

266
00:33:29,971 --> 00:33:33,641
It's more fair, Zöhre Hatun!

267
00:33:34,597 --> 00:33:38,717
Come on, Alps!
Ya Allah!

268
00:35:09,488 --> 00:35:12,548
Dündar Bey will make his aides treat.

269
00:35:13,420 --> 00:35:17,295
Osman punished me, by keeping Balgay.

270
00:35:17,295 --> 00:35:22,545
I'll save Dündar and do what
Balgay can't do.

271
00:35:23,248 --> 00:35:25,441
I'll kill Osman.

272
00:35:25,441 --> 00:35:29,271
I'll have both Dündar and the Kayıs.

273
00:35:37,451 --> 00:35:42,320
Tell me about your betrayal, Zöhre.

274
00:35:42,320 --> 00:35:45,600
It's not over yet, Hatun.

275
00:35:45,861 --> 00:35:49,711
Dündar Bey will call you to account.

276
00:35:49,894 --> 00:35:53,094
Dündar Bey drowned in his treason.

277
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:57,469
I killed him, Zöhre Hatun.

278
00:35:57,469 --> 00:35:59,289
Father.

279
00:36:11,875 --> 00:36:13,995
Dündar.

280
00:36:29,040 --> 00:36:34,110
You killed both my son and husband, Osman.

281
00:36:35,579 --> 00:36:42,249
Dündar Bey and Batur collaborated
Mongols and Balgay.

282
00:36:42,694 --> 00:36:45,234
They betrayed Kayıs.

283
00:36:45,265 --> 00:36:49,555
Did you think I'd let traitors live?

284
00:36:55,609 --> 00:36:59,459
The Bey of our tent is still my father.

285
00:37:00,357 --> 00:37:05,827
No one can disobey our morals and our Bey.

286
00:37:10,315 --> 00:37:12,485
Tell everyone...

287
00:37:13,107 --> 00:37:18,547
I killed Dündar Bey myself.

288
00:37:19,755 --> 00:37:21,745
Murderer.

289
00:37:29,509 --> 00:37:31,949
Take Zöhre Hatun to the tent.

290
00:37:33,527 --> 00:37:35,667
To the cage.

291
00:37:37,016 --> 00:37:39,591
I have a bone to pick with her.

292
00:37:39,591 --> 00:37:42,341
Let me go!

293
00:37:42,681 --> 00:37:46,521
You'll get your deserts, Osman!

294
00:37:46,698 --> 00:37:49,838
You killed my father and brother.

295
00:37:50,416 --> 00:37:54,006
Murderer. Shame on you!

296
00:37:55,722 --> 00:37:58,102
Shame on you!

297
00:38:04,055 --> 00:38:06,208
Shame on you!

298
00:38:06,208 --> 00:38:09,278
Take Aygül too.
Come on.

299
00:38:09,658 --> 00:38:11,097
Come on.

300
00:38:18,493 --> 00:38:22,833
Zülfikar Dervish, take my
brother to the tent.

301
00:38:24,119 --> 00:38:26,409
Listen to me now.

302
00:38:44,693 --> 00:38:48,180
Abdurrahman Ghazi! Dündar Bey!

303
00:38:51,300 --> 00:38:52,930
Dündar!

304
00:38:59,719 --> 00:39:04,019
He's in a bad condition. We
need to stop bleeding.

305
00:39:04,463 --> 00:39:06,633
Build a fire.

306
00:39:10,528 --> 00:39:14,728
We need to take the arrow out.
Give me the dagger.

307
00:39:18,510 --> 00:39:22,250
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. ( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

308
00:39:22,556 --> 00:39:26,666
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. ( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

309
00:39:28,052 --> 00:39:29,402
O The Healer.

310
00:39:31,926 --> 00:39:36,476
Should we attack? They're six, three
of them are wounded.

311
00:39:39,075 --> 00:39:43,955
It's time, my Bey, if you let me.

312
00:39:44,535 --> 00:39:47,895
You don't know Abdurrahman Ghazi.

313
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:51,370
His beard is gray...

314
00:39:51,421 --> 00:39:52,681
O The Healer.

315
00:39:52,778 --> 00:39:57,028
But when it comes to
war, he's like a dragon.

316
00:39:57,727 --> 00:40:01,097
Melik, tell the scouts.

317
00:40:01,171 --> 00:40:05,141
Tell them to come here with warriors who
are capable of using the weapons well.

318
00:40:10,314 --> 00:40:14,784
Zorba, keep an eye on them.

319
00:40:29,151 --> 00:40:31,382
Will he be okay, Abdurrahman Ghazi?

320
00:40:31,382 --> 00:40:32,912
Inshaallah.

321
00:40:33,955 --> 00:40:36,125
But he's still bleeding...

322
00:40:36,164 --> 00:40:38,534
we should cauterise.

323
00:40:39,082 --> 00:40:42,432
O The Healer.
O The Healer.

324
00:40:42,478 --> 00:40:44,158
O The Healer.

325
00:42:11,602 --> 00:42:12,782
Cerkutay.

326
00:42:17,439 --> 00:42:19,209
Balgay, you're wounded.

327
00:42:23,078 --> 00:42:25,368
Osman kept his powder dry.

328
00:42:25,716 --> 00:42:28,316
If we passed the hill...

329
00:42:28,736 --> 00:42:31,456
we would have been under attack now.

330
00:42:48,267 --> 00:42:51,457
How can Osman do that, Balgay?

331
00:42:52,316 --> 00:42:55,966
We underestimated our enemy.

332
00:43:09,822 --> 00:43:12,692
I swear on Kanbukan...

333
00:43:15,906 --> 00:43:18,356
I swear on...

334
00:43:19,019 --> 00:43:20,929
this fire.

335
00:43:22,383 --> 00:43:25,073
My revenge will be hard.

336
00:43:25,130 --> 00:43:28,840
How could Osman set this trap, Balgay?

337
00:43:28,975 --> 00:43:30,815
Yannis!

338
00:43:33,151 --> 00:43:37,921
Apparently, that old one also forgot
the Mongol's anger.

339
00:43:38,837 --> 00:43:41,687
If he hadn't collaborated with Osman...

340
00:43:41,687 --> 00:43:44,927
Osman would be bleeding now.

341
00:43:47,260 --> 00:43:49,930
We ran out of soldiers, Balgay.

342
00:43:50,153 --> 00:43:52,553
What will we do if Geyhatu hears that?

343
00:43:52,732 --> 00:43:56,732
This is now my war.

344
00:43:58,313 --> 00:44:02,433
If he faces me, I will kill Geyhatu.

345
00:44:08,925 --> 00:44:11,315
We will go to Konya.

346
00:44:11,390 --> 00:44:16,170
We will get new soldiers and come back.

347
00:44:18,825 --> 00:44:21,235
When we come back...

348
00:44:21,410 --> 00:44:24,700
we will kill everyone.

349
00:44:26,923 --> 00:44:29,733
We will kill...

350
00:44:32,553 --> 00:44:37,213
everyone in this country.

351
00:45:47,608 --> 00:45:49,838
When you are a child...

352
00:45:50,527 --> 00:45:53,487
you think your father is...

353
00:45:54,439 --> 00:45:57,389
undefeated, the strongest.

354
00:45:59,139 --> 00:46:03,139
You think you'll defeat everyone
when you grow up...

355
00:46:03,984 --> 00:46:06,954
like your father.

356
00:46:08,869 --> 00:46:11,699
You fight many battles...

357
00:46:16,642 --> 00:46:20,642
but you lose against a beatiful one.

358
00:46:38,886 --> 00:46:42,196
Thank my Lord, I can live this moment.

359
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:54,230
Gonca is waiting.
I should go.

360
00:46:54,759 --> 00:46:56,169
Okay, daughter.

361
00:47:14,594 --> 00:47:17,924
I know you have a lot of responsiblities.

362
00:47:18,901 --> 00:47:21,131
You are always in a war.

363
00:47:21,934 --> 00:47:23,124
However...

364
00:47:24,112 --> 00:47:27,642
Not only that,
there's something else.

365
00:47:28,036 --> 00:47:29,166
Tell me.

366
00:47:31,220 --> 00:47:32,300
You are right.

367
00:47:34,488 --> 00:47:36,428
You are right, mother.

368
00:47:37,927 --> 00:47:38,747
What?

369
00:47:40,354 --> 00:47:42,354
It is Bala.

370
00:47:43,726 --> 00:47:45,186
What happened to Bala?

371
00:47:45,542 --> 00:47:47,192
She changed.

372
00:47:47,543 --> 00:47:49,693
She became someone else.

373
00:47:50,019 --> 00:47:52,749
She says she is done for me.

374
00:47:53,150 --> 00:47:56,780
- She tells me to look another Hatun.
- Did Bala tell you that?

375
00:47:56,829 --> 00:47:59,519
Yes.
Bala told me.

376
00:48:00,654 --> 00:48:05,744
Bala, who I put in the middle of my
heart, told that to me, mother.

377
00:48:08,485 --> 00:48:11,695
Why, son, why did she?

378
00:48:14,459 --> 00:48:17,259
I am looking for the answer.

379
00:48:18,661 --> 00:48:20,808
I insisted...

380
00:48:20,808 --> 00:48:24,568
I pushed her, but she doesn't talk.

381
00:48:24,590 --> 00:48:27,990
There's something else,
but she won't tell me.

382
00:48:36,375 --> 00:48:38,545
You can learn.

383
00:48:38,567 --> 00:48:41,237
Tell me when you learn.

384
00:48:41,625 --> 00:48:46,455
If it is a vaild reason,
Eyvallah ( it's okay)

385
00:48:47,620 --> 00:48:50,660
If she says she doesn't love me anymore...

386
00:48:53,551 --> 00:48:55,551
Eyvallah ( it's also okay)

387
00:49:40,334 --> 00:49:43,044
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

388
00:50:01,245 --> 00:50:03,258
Why did you do that to me?

389
00:50:03,258 --> 00:50:08,778
You, how did you do that to our tribe,
our Ertuğrul Bey, Dündar Bey?

390
00:50:11,444 --> 00:50:14,454
A great pain in the grave is waiting
for you.

391
00:50:15,204 --> 00:50:17,684
I pity you.

392
00:50:19,147 --> 00:50:24,630
You killed my son, my Batur.

393
00:50:24,630 --> 00:50:27,310
Did you believe that?

394
00:50:27,719 --> 00:50:33,189
Like you believed Alişar, Balgay, Sofia.

395
00:50:34,202 --> 00:50:37,142
Ah, Dündar Bey, ah.

396
00:50:45,785 --> 00:50:48,515
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

397
00:50:50,308 --> 00:50:52,628
Kill me.

398
00:50:53,232 --> 00:50:55,152
Kill me.

399
00:50:55,462 --> 00:51:01,732
Or I will kill all of you.

400
00:51:05,634 --> 00:51:10,374
I will take revenge of my son Batur.

401
00:51:10,847 --> 00:51:13,217
Kill me.

402
00:51:13,499 --> 00:51:18,149
Who sent you to where Osman set
a trap for Balgay? Tell me.

403
00:51:18,543 --> 00:51:22,983
Tell me so that Osman can reveal the
game against us.

404
00:51:23,064 --> 00:51:27,284
Then you can have the answers.

405
00:51:28,079 --> 00:51:30,849
The game is Osman.

406
00:51:34,293 --> 00:51:36,193
Osman.

407
00:51:56,053 --> 00:51:58,463
It's Osman's command.

408
00:51:59,519 --> 00:52:07,059
In order for him to atten his son's funeral
we'll take him to the graveyard tomorrow.

409
00:52:11,444 --> 00:52:13,576
I will be with him.

410
00:52:13,576 --> 00:52:16,456
- Inshallah he gets better until tomorrow.
- Inshallah.

411
00:52:38,130 --> 00:52:45,100
Go, go away,cheeky Hatun, I see
blood while looking at you!

412
00:52:45,990 --> 00:52:49,460
It's the blood you shed, Zöhre.

413
00:52:49,710 --> 00:52:52,650
- You think of what you did.
- Enough!

414
00:52:53,167 --> 00:52:56,012
Enough of your injustice!

415
00:52:56,012 --> 00:52:59,072
Look, what is your daughter saying?

416
00:52:59,162 --> 00:53:01,302
She says enough.

417
00:53:01,723 --> 00:53:03,973
Enough already.

418
00:53:03,973 --> 00:53:07,323
First Bala, now Gündüz.

419
00:53:07,811 --> 00:53:12,131
This is not coincidence.
Speak!

420
00:53:13,111 --> 00:53:17,239
You are out of your mind!

421
00:53:17,239 --> 00:53:20,119
You are greedy for power!

422
00:53:20,718 --> 00:53:24,641
Take it.
The tribe and Beyship is yours!

423
00:53:24,641 --> 00:53:31,355
However, I will take revenge of my
Batur and Dündar!

424
00:53:31,355 --> 00:53:33,825
What are you going to do, Zöhre?

425
00:53:36,306 --> 00:53:38,746
Will you seek help from Mongols?

426
00:54:01,441 --> 00:54:04,781
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.)

427
00:54:04,941 --> 00:54:07,841
He is capable of everything...

428
00:54:08,023 --> 00:54:16,103
he fills our hearts with faith.
With the great Allah's 99 names.

429
00:54:19,163 --> 00:54:21,433
My valiant fellows.

430
00:54:21,468 --> 00:54:23,738
My tribe's almighty ones.

431
00:54:26,073 --> 00:54:33,893
My uncle Dündar's Beyship has ended.
He bowed his head for Mongols.

432
00:54:39,433 --> 00:54:43,607
Everybody saw that...

433
00:54:43,607 --> 00:54:49,817
Not the ones who obey Mongols...

434
00:54:50,177 --> 00:54:56,817
The ones who bow their head against no
one will be the future of Kayı!

435
00:55:04,309 --> 00:55:12,989
Now, until my father returns, one of the
Kayı Beys will take his place.

436
00:55:14,613 --> 00:55:19,023
I want that we choose a Bey...

437
00:55:19,063 --> 00:55:26,733
who is going to be a servant for his
people, and be cruel to the enemy!

438
00:55:32,529 --> 00:55:38,349
Osman Bey.
What you do is not in our tradition.

439
00:55:38,405 --> 00:55:42,465
You spared our lives, Eyvallah (thank you)

440
00:55:42,516 --> 00:55:49,376
However, just because you spared our lives,
we can't ignore our tradition.

441
00:55:49,507 --> 00:55:58,328
Şahin Bey is right. The candidates should
be determiend beforehand.

442
00:56:03,449 --> 00:56:07,829
Beys.
Beys.

443
00:56:09,321 --> 00:56:15,301
Look at the ones who talk about
tradiiton.

444
00:56:18,665 --> 00:56:21,885
Demirci Bey.
Şahin Bey.

445
00:56:22,564 --> 00:56:28,074
Who bowes their head for gold from
Mongols...

446
00:56:29,048 --> 00:56:32,428
can't question our tradition.

447
00:56:33,968 --> 00:56:37,200
We are talking about tradition, Bamsı Bey.

448
00:56:37,200 --> 00:56:42,090
Neither our intention is bad,
nor what we say is wrong.

449
00:56:49,348 --> 00:56:52,689
Don't abuse Osman Bey's mercy.

450
00:56:52,689 --> 00:56:55,459
The format is right.

451
00:56:56,573 --> 00:57:03,373
There will be a election.
We'll choose a Bey, and obey.

452
00:57:09,921 --> 00:57:13,522
Şahin Bey, Demirci Bey.

453
00:57:13,522 --> 00:57:15,672
Don't panic.

454
00:57:16,710 --> 00:57:21,450
There wouldn't be impropriety
where my brother stands.

455
00:57:21,498 --> 00:57:24,988
However, know that...

456
00:57:25,838 --> 00:57:31,378
who disgraces the tradition
has nothing to do in this tribe.

457
00:57:42,821 --> 00:57:45,415
My father set everything right.

458
00:57:45,415 --> 00:57:48,255
Osman had to interfere!

459
00:57:48,308 --> 00:57:51,984
My brother is gone.
My father is gone!

460
00:57:51,984 --> 00:57:55,194
Will you take my mother now?

461
00:57:57,366 --> 00:58:02,456
This is your time to be seen nice
in Osman's sight.

462
00:58:02,547 --> 00:58:05,537
Kill me and my mother.

463
00:58:06,320 --> 00:58:09,150
You can be the new owners.

464
00:58:10,679 --> 00:58:12,979
Shame on you.

465
00:58:14,951 --> 00:58:19,751
The more someone is angry the worse
her heart is.

466
00:58:20,175 --> 00:58:22,815
She becoems rude, Aygül Hatun.

467
00:58:23,415 --> 00:58:26,185
I wish you could hear what you say.

468
00:58:27,511 --> 00:58:29,541
Ah, ah.

469
00:58:32,418 --> 00:58:36,888
Now, I will say it directly, Zöhre Hatun.

470
00:58:37,643 --> 00:58:40,683
There will be Batur's funeral.

471
00:58:40,917 --> 00:58:45,264
If you wish to be a mother and
attend to the funeral...

472
00:58:45,264 --> 00:58:50,924
I can get you out of here.

473
00:58:52,920 --> 00:58:57,067
Tell me.
Are you coming or not?

474
00:58:57,067 --> 00:59:02,797
What do you mean coming or not?
Of course I will come.

475
00:59:02,797 --> 00:59:05,807
Of course I will!

476
00:59:13,113 --> 00:59:15,173
Okay then.

477
00:59:17,284 --> 00:59:20,529
I know your heart is burning.

478
00:59:20,529 --> 00:59:22,804
I know your situation.

479
00:59:22,804 --> 00:59:27,344
However, if you wish to attend
Batur's funeral...

480
00:59:28,769 --> 00:59:31,909
you need to speak.

481
00:59:34,500 --> 00:59:40,445
We understand, we know that you
are involved in this.

482
00:59:40,445 --> 00:59:43,505
We need further information.

483
00:59:43,505 --> 00:59:48,995
Tell me, then we can go to the funeral,
ha?

484
00:59:49,572 --> 00:59:51,032
Speak.

485
00:59:52,587 --> 00:59:54,917
Come on, Zöhre.

486
00:59:54,917 --> 00:59:57,597
Give it away.

487
00:59:58,209 --> 01:00:02,509
Be with your son.
Tell me.

488
01:00:06,495 --> 01:00:08,975
I wanted to save it.

489
01:00:10,177 --> 01:00:14,617
I wanted to protect my children, my Bey.

490
01:00:15,727 --> 01:00:19,157
I did it to protect my tribe.

491
01:00:20,353 --> 01:00:22,523
Tell me.

492
01:00:26,778 --> 01:00:29,028
I went to Balgay.

493
01:00:38,271 --> 01:00:40,521
Mother.

494
01:00:41,014 --> 01:00:44,014
What have you done?

495
01:01:06,078 --> 01:01:10,568
I asked, your mother talked, Aygül.

496
01:01:10,745 --> 01:01:13,065
You heard.

497
01:01:13,793 --> 01:01:16,333
I have had enough.

498
01:01:17,394 --> 01:01:19,844
You can tell the rest to your daughter.

499
01:01:32,469 --> 01:01:34,049
Gonca.

500
01:01:39,986 --> 01:01:43,116
What does Bala Hatun worry about?

501
01:01:44,211 --> 01:01:50,751
Tell me. She told Osman to look for another woman.
Is this because of her problems?

502
01:01:57,670 --> 01:02:01,970
It's because of her wound which she's
received in Mongol attack.

503
01:02:07,109 --> 01:02:09,699
She won't have any children from now on.

504
01:02:19,392 --> 01:02:23,562
Now that the intention is to choose
a bey to correct the law...

505
01:02:23,923 --> 01:02:27,923
...then everybody should speak.

506
01:02:28,308 --> 01:02:32,308
Now, Kayı Tent is not the same as before.

507
01:02:32,544 --> 01:02:35,914
We have a lot of flocks and products.

508
01:02:36,421 --> 01:02:43,551
We need a bey that needs to
carry out both trade and morals.

509
01:02:48,270 --> 01:02:49,740
My candidate is...

510
01:02:52,803 --> 01:02:54,463
...Gunduz Bey.

511
01:03:05,505 --> 01:03:11,485
He is sincere, graceful and his
decisions are proper.

512
01:03:13,506 --> 01:03:14,916
My candidate is...

513
01:03:16,751 --> 01:03:18,151
...Gunduz Bey.

514
01:03:31,781 --> 01:03:35,291
We've got over all those problems
thanks to his determination.

515
01:03:35,408 --> 01:03:39,408
We've got over tough circumstances
thanks to his skillfulness.

516
01:03:39,872 --> 01:03:43,872
I like Gunduz Bey so much and
appreciate him a lot.

517
01:03:45,698 --> 01:03:49,698
But I think Osman Bey should be
the bey of all Kayı Tents.

518
01:03:57,800 --> 01:03:59,910
My candidate is Osman Bey.

519
01:04:10,573 --> 01:04:13,023
I agree with Sahin Bey and Demirci Bey.

520
01:04:13,111 --> 01:04:15,241
My candidate is Gunduz Bey.

521
01:04:29,693 --> 01:04:30,763
My Osman...

522
01:04:32,021 --> 01:04:33,731
My Osman is the flood.

523
01:04:36,343 --> 01:04:38,233
And Gunduz is the soil.

524
01:04:39,992 --> 01:04:41,512
My Osman is the water.

525
01:04:42,767 --> 01:04:44,467
My Gunduz is the bread.

526
01:04:46,914 --> 01:04:49,684
My Osman is the fire.

527
01:04:51,639 --> 01:04:53,699
My Gunduz is the coolness.

528
01:04:56,211 --> 01:04:57,281
But...

529
01:04:58,325 --> 01:05:02,205
...bey is such a person that
he foresees the future

530
01:05:03,684 --> 01:05:08,364
Bey is such a person that he has
blood on both side of the sword.

531
01:05:11,255 --> 01:05:12,185
So...

532
01:05:19,079 --> 01:05:23,959
...my candidate is Osman.

533
01:05:24,165 --> 01:05:25,735
Osman bey.

534
01:05:36,575 --> 01:05:37,535
Bamsi Bey.

535
01:05:37,635 --> 01:05:39,425
The right is speaking.

536
01:05:39,511 --> 01:05:41,431
My candidate is Osman Bey.

537
01:05:49,936 --> 01:05:51,606
We stopped.

538
01:05:53,416 --> 01:05:54,696
He ran.

539
01:05:56,052 --> 01:05:57,282
We just looked.

540
01:05:59,302 --> 01:06:00,412
He hit.

541
01:06:01,579 --> 01:06:03,409
There had been occupations.

542
01:06:05,928 --> 01:06:07,448
We all obeyed them.

543
01:06:11,020 --> 01:06:12,640
He rose against them.

544
01:06:14,186 --> 01:06:17,656
He has been our hope, our freedom and
our honour.

545
01:06:17,784 --> 01:06:20,464
He isn't just a brother for me...

546
01:06:21,407 --> 01:06:23,327
...he is my fellow always.

547
01:06:25,366 --> 01:06:30,286
I see the ability that my Father had,
not in me.

548
01:06:33,309 --> 01:06:35,089
I see it in him.

549
01:06:37,610 --> 01:06:39,730
I know and believe that...

550
01:06:40,173 --> 01:06:44,173
...the prosperity of Kayı is Osman.

551
01:06:49,986 --> 01:06:51,366
My candidate is...

552
01:06:51,995 --> 01:06:53,655
...Osman.

553
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:19,250
Duty is both hard and holy.

554
01:07:20,201 --> 01:07:27,261
My brother is both careful and	moderate.

555
01:07:30,595 --> 01:07:37,705
In this tough process, we need
a fair bey who foresees the future...

556
01:07:38,622 --> 01:07:45,252
...who is calm, graceful
and acts according to his morals.

557
01:07:47,089 --> 01:07:49,439
My brother Gunduz Bey...

558
01:07:49,907 --> 01:07:53,397
...has the ability to differentiate
the black snake on the black stone...

559
01:07:53,577 --> 01:07:58,177
...has the ability to differentiate
the white material in white milk.

560
01:08:05,469 --> 01:08:06,869
My candidate is...

561
01:08:10,475 --> 01:08:12,725
...my brother Gunduz bey.

562
01:08:21,205 --> 01:08:24,515
I renounce from all votes.

563
01:08:24,648 --> 01:08:30,648
My brother Gunduz bey is
the bey of Ertugrul Gazi.

564
01:08:47,844 --> 01:08:50,594
I wish best for your Tent, my brother.

565
01:10:57,160 --> 01:10:59,510
I wish best for your Tent, my brother.

566
01:11:00,653 --> 01:11:02,183
Thanks, brother.

567
01:11:16,713 --> 01:11:19,853
I wish you will bring luck to soldiers,
Gunduz Bey.

568
01:11:22,540 --> 01:11:23,710
Thanks, Samsa.

569
01:11:27,344 --> 01:11:30,794
If you excuse me,
I want to go my tent

570
01:11:30,874 --> 01:11:33,474
I need to check it.

571
01:11:33,598 --> 01:11:35,468
You can go, Samsa Bey.

572
01:11:54,350 --> 01:11:56,840
I wish best for your Tent, Gunduz Bey.

573
01:11:58,443 --> 01:11:59,563
Thanks.

574
01:12:06,536 --> 01:12:09,556
I wish best for your Tent, Gunduz Bey.

575
01:12:10,521 --> 01:12:11,401
Thanks.

576
01:12:25,829 --> 01:12:27,819
I wish best for your Tent, my son.

577
01:12:33,043 --> 01:12:34,473
Thanks, Bamsi Bey.

578
01:13:23,997 --> 01:13:24,897
Batur.

579
01:13:31,502 --> 01:13:37,722
In the first day he joined our case,
his bravery was nearly led him to death.

580
01:13:39,258 --> 01:13:40,628
Our road
was separate.

581
01:13:42,379 --> 01:13:47,119
But Allah is witness, his intention
wasn't bad.

582
01:13:49,718 --> 01:13:55,128
If he hadn't stand behind his father,
his ending wouldn't be like that.

583
01:14:00,129 --> 01:14:04,489
I'll cut the heads of those
who did it to you, myself.

584
01:14:05,607 --> 01:14:06,847
I promise.

585
01:14:08,261 --> 01:14:09,791
Son.

586
01:14:09,947 --> 01:14:11,837
You will take your revenge.

587
01:14:11,915 --> 01:14:12,865
You will.

588
01:14:12,952 --> 01:14:14,052
But from who?

589
01:14:14,317 --> 01:14:16,037
Who did this treachery?

590
01:14:19,173 --> 01:14:21,233
I don't know who planned it
now.

591
01:14:22,209 --> 01:14:26,299
But those who set up traps think that they
reached their goal.

592
01:14:27,330 --> 01:14:30,920
They wanted you to be
responsible for this job.

593
01:14:31,042 --> 01:14:32,912
And they got what they wanted.

594
01:14:32,945 --> 01:14:35,755
I'll ruin all the
traps they set.

595
01:14:37,746 --> 01:14:42,546
Now that they don't act properly,
I will act like them.

596
01:14:43,243 --> 01:14:47,343
Is it the reason why you hide that Dundar
is alive, my son?

597
01:14:48,199 --> 01:14:52,199
Let those who set up
traps believe they are winning!

598
01:14:53,129 --> 01:14:55,149
Let them believe more.

599
01:14:55,801 --> 01:15:01,941
I'll disintegrate this foggy air with a wolf
claw where even devil acts like a Muslim.

600
01:15:03,803 --> 01:15:08,363
Till that day, let them know
that I killed Batur.

601
01:15:09,499 --> 01:15:11,269
When the time is over...

602
01:15:11,846 --> 01:15:16,246
...I'll kill and cut the heads of
those evils.

603
01:15:17,381 --> 01:15:19,341
What about Dundar?

604
01:15:21,516 --> 01:15:30,166
Dundar bey has the right to be here
when his son is buried, Bamsi Bey.

605
01:15:31,739 --> 01:15:32,909
I reported.

606
01:15:33,101 --> 01:15:36,131
Abdullah Efendi will bring him to the tent
before the funeral.

607
01:15:37,004 --> 01:15:38,584
Thanks, Osman.

608
01:15:38,807 --> 01:15:39,597
Thanks.

609
01:15:46,407 --> 01:15:47,207
My bey.

610
01:15:47,487 --> 01:15:48,767
Balgay escaped.

611
01:15:49,076 --> 01:15:52,586
The only way Balgay can escape
is his death.

612
01:15:53,527 --> 01:15:55,437
He can't get rid of me.

613
01:16:16,089 --> 01:16:17,779
You ruined.

614
01:16:18,459 --> 01:16:20,199
You exhausted yourself.

615
01:16:21,011 --> 01:16:22,871
Don't do it anymore.

616
01:16:24,746 --> 01:16:26,316
I can't bear to...

617
01:16:28,855 --> 01:16:31,005
...be silence when he speaks...

618
01:16:32,604 --> 01:16:35,884
...go away when he is approaching...

619
01:16:41,734 --> 01:16:44,454
...and offend him deliberately every time,
Gonca.

620
01:16:47,692 --> 01:16:49,452
That doesn't work like that.

621
01:16:50,172 --> 01:16:51,862
That doesn't work like that, Bala.

622
01:16:52,829 --> 01:16:56,829
If you don't say it to Osman,
I will.

623
01:16:58,516 --> 01:17:00,716
You're not gonna say anything.

624
01:17:03,862 --> 01:17:06,042
We'll go from here.

625
01:17:07,669 --> 01:17:09,919
It will be better to not be here.

626
01:17:16,759 --> 01:17:18,419
What's happened, my mother?

627
01:17:18,945 --> 01:17:21,225
Why are you sad, explain to me?

628
01:17:22,008 --> 01:17:23,658
I will, my son.

629
01:17:24,283 --> 01:17:25,473
Is it about Bala?

630
01:17:25,985 --> 01:17:27,435
Tell me, mother.

631
01:17:30,463 --> 01:17:32,863
Bala has a big trouble, my son.

632
01:17:32,990 --> 01:17:36,600
She lives with the hardest
trouble any woman ever can have.

633
01:17:36,745 --> 01:17:37,845
What's that?

634
01:17:39,086 --> 01:17:40,026
Explain.

635
01:17:40,683 --> 01:17:41,973
Explain, mother.

636
01:17:42,105 --> 01:17:43,435
Don't worry me.

637
01:17:47,290 --> 01:17:50,070
The wound she got
when Mongol attacked...

638
01:17:52,774 --> 01:17:55,674
...is the reason of coldness
between you, my son.

639
01:17:58,579 --> 01:18:01,269
It isn't because she doesn't
love you.

640
01:18:06,142 --> 01:18:11,782
As she fears that she can't give birth
to a baby, she spoke you like that.

641
01:18:19,088 --> 01:18:20,368
But...

642
01:18:21,238 --> 01:18:22,678
It is not certain.

643
01:18:27,789 --> 01:18:32,789
I can't leave her
just because of this.

644
01:18:34,008 --> 01:18:35,348
I know, my son.

645
01:18:35,728 --> 01:18:36,928
I know.

646
01:18:37,652 --> 01:18:41,362
Your love is as strong as
your heart.

647
01:18:45,997 --> 01:18:48,157
The caretaker of
Bala told her...

648
01:18:48,988 --> 01:18:52,988
...she shouldn't give up from believing
Allah after the wound she got.

649
01:18:53,434 --> 01:18:56,174
She won't give up surely.

650
01:18:56,521 --> 01:18:58,621
But she hesitates a lot.

651
01:18:59,867 --> 01:19:03,867
Nobody knows how much she got
worried and thought about it.

652
01:19:06,996 --> 01:19:09,056
I wish I forced her more.

653
01:19:09,799 --> 01:19:11,929
I wish I knew it before.

654
01:19:12,222 --> 01:19:14,942
She may have thought about it
a lot.

655
01:19:17,115 --> 01:19:20,295
But now it's the problem
both of you.

656
01:19:21,844 --> 01:19:25,844
You can sacrifice your life for
each other let alone love each other.

657
01:19:29,807 --> 01:19:30,807
I know.

658
01:19:30,943 --> 01:19:33,123
You'll get rid of it eventually.

659
01:19:35,259 --> 01:19:37,459
You again made me a favour
as my mother.

660
01:19:37,997 --> 01:19:39,567
You relieved me.

661
01:19:40,943 --> 01:19:43,323
You learned the truth for me.

662
01:19:45,429 --> 01:19:48,619
May Allah don't allow us
to be far apart, my mother.

663
01:19:50,505 --> 01:19:52,225
Don't allow us.

664
01:20:15,502 --> 01:20:16,952
Walk!

665
01:20:22,000 --> 01:20:24,000
Where are you taking me?

666
01:20:24,571 --> 01:20:26,331
Why isn't there anyone?

667
01:20:26,712 --> 01:20:28,702
They went to revenge Balgay.

668
01:20:29,604 --> 01:20:30,464
How?

669
01:20:31,383 --> 01:20:33,873
How dare they?

670
01:20:34,094 --> 01:20:36,154
You don't know Osman Bey.

671
01:20:36,289 --> 01:20:39,179
Everything happened thanks to you
and Yannis, Sofia.

672
01:20:40,581 --> 01:20:41,931
Walk!

673
01:20:50,939 --> 01:20:52,579
Traitor Salvador!

674
01:21:11,595 --> 01:21:12,455
Salvador.

675
01:21:12,728 --> 01:21:14,588
You are free now, princess.

676
01:21:15,918 --> 01:21:18,128
Where is Helen and Andreas?

677
01:21:19,742 --> 01:21:23,002
Andreas died when he was trying to escape.

678
01:21:24,706 --> 01:21:26,336
Helen is waiting for us.

679
01:21:30,280 --> 01:21:31,380
Salvador.

680
01:21:32,990 --> 01:21:34,950
I will never forget it.

681
01:21:49,258 --> 01:21:51,058
You get just your desserts.

682
01:21:52,671 --> 01:21:53,791
Dervish.

683
01:22:00,066 --> 01:22:02,636
Let's take Helen and go
back to the castle.

684
01:22:32,400 --> 01:22:33,610
Who are you?

685
01:22:33,935 --> 01:22:35,245
Your death.

686
01:22:37,558 --> 01:22:41,118
I've seen a lot of brave people wishing
to be my death.

687
01:22:42,042 --> 01:22:44,332
But all of them are dead.

688
01:22:51,449 --> 01:22:53,209
Abdurrahman Gazi!

689
01:23:00,922 --> 01:23:02,482
Alps!

690
01:23:07,927 --> 01:23:10,047
Allahu Akbar!

691
01:23:31,116 --> 01:23:32,606
Kılıç!

692
01:23:36,883 --> 01:23:38,293
Kılıç!

693
01:23:40,636 --> 01:23:41,806
Erkut!

694
01:23:51,005 --> 01:23:52,135
My valiant!

695
01:23:52,372 --> 01:23:53,932
Abdurrahman Gazi!

696
01:23:54,449 --> 01:23:55,929
Kılıç!

697
01:23:57,135 --> 01:23:58,175
Erkut!

698
01:23:58,676 --> 01:24:03,436
I bear witness that...
there is none worthy of worship except Allah...

699
01:24:12,499 --> 01:24:14,009
Alişar!

700
01:24:18,541 --> 01:24:20,011
Alişar!

701
01:24:20,267 --> 01:24:21,507
You, huh?

702
01:24:26,494 --> 01:24:29,264
Alişar! You, huh?

703
01:24:33,158 --> 01:24:40,108
Leaving Dundar bey for such jackals like
you doesn't suit to banner lord like me.

704
01:24:40,108 --> 01:24:43,148
Instead of hiding behind your soldiers...

705
01:24:43,148 --> 01:24:46,368
... come and fight with me like
a real man. Come, Alisar!

706
01:25:06,006 --> 01:25:07,786
Abdurrahman Gazi.

707
01:25:41,327 --> 01:25:45,987
As long as you have such a heart,
everything will be alright eventually.

708
01:25:56,599 --> 01:26:00,189
- Welcome, my girl.
- Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

709
01:26:08,002 --> 01:26:12,002
I was going to take some syrup.
Let me prepare it. We will drink together.

710
01:26:26,657 --> 01:26:29,397
Like I don't love anybody except you...

711
01:26:30,263 --> 01:26:33,663
...I don't have the intention of
looking for someone else, Bala.

712
01:26:35,502 --> 01:26:37,492
You are my blessing.

713
01:26:41,365 --> 01:26:42,695
Just be.

714
01:26:44,490 --> 01:26:46,760
Having a child is the will of Allah.

715
01:26:54,975 --> 01:26:57,405
As we love each other like that...

716
01:26:57,905 --> 01:27:01,905
...the power of a dagger wound
can't tear us apart, Bala.

717
01:27:03,108 --> 01:27:04,558
Osman.

718
01:27:08,221 --> 01:27:09,411
Don't.

719
01:27:10,921 --> 01:27:11,821
No.

720
01:27:13,833 --> 01:27:15,923
You will have children.

721
01:27:17,267 --> 01:27:18,837
I'm not suitable for you.

722
01:27:18,837 --> 01:27:20,347
Are you not suitable for me?

723
01:27:20,750 --> 01:27:24,260
Bala! Being without you breaks me
down.

724
01:27:25,211 --> 01:27:28,911
Being without you is the biggest
problem between now and tomorrow.

725
01:27:32,438 --> 01:27:37,988
You are my strength and power.

726
01:27:38,707 --> 01:27:40,697
You're the light of my road.

727
01:27:42,251 --> 01:27:43,251
You...

728
01:27:45,321 --> 01:27:48,961
... are my dream. My love.

729
01:27:52,262 --> 01:27:55,202
After gaining my sheikh consent...

730
01:27:56,130 --> 01:27:59,240
... having a family with you
is my biggest dream.

731
01:28:06,366 --> 01:28:08,856
You're my blind love, Hatun.

732
01:28:12,694 --> 01:28:20,504
If Allah doesn't give us
a child, I am okay with that.

733
01:28:22,419 --> 01:28:25,219
I am okay with everything as long
as I'm with you.

734
01:28:27,949 --> 01:28:29,219
Tell me.

735
01:28:31,067 --> 01:28:32,947
Are you okay with it too?

736
01:28:37,626 --> 01:28:42,116
I accept everything as long
as you do, Osman.

737
01:28:48,222 --> 01:28:50,102
May I come in, my Bey?

738
01:28:54,433 --> 01:28:56,263
Come in, Boran.

739
01:28:58,626 --> 01:29:00,156
Excuse me.

740
01:29:06,593 --> 01:29:10,593
My Bey, a valiant wants to see you.
He says it is important.

741
01:29:11,759 --> 01:29:13,699
He may come in.

742
01:29:27,948 --> 01:29:30,198
Where are you headed to, Osman Bey?

743
01:29:33,608 --> 01:29:35,318
To Kızıl Elma.

744
01:29:43,632 --> 01:29:46,312
The Elders are waiting for you, Osman Bey.

745
01:29:47,086 --> 01:29:49,036
Your duty is important.

746
01:30:17,822 --> 01:30:19,712
We have failed, Master.

747
01:30:23,040 --> 01:30:24,310
Forgive us.

748
01:30:40,607 --> 01:30:46,147
What's important is that you're still
here, my daughter.

749
01:30:49,751 --> 01:30:52,931
You made an agreement with
Osman for me, Master.

750
01:30:55,320 --> 01:30:57,050
You shouldn't have done it.

751
01:30:57,050 --> 01:31:01,050
I can turn these lands into
a sea of blood for you.

752
01:31:04,861 --> 01:31:06,551
Where is Andreas?

753
01:31:08,397 --> 01:31:11,607
They...
They killed him, Master.

754
01:31:14,743 --> 01:31:18,743
What is that called?
Stupidity? Or betrayal?

755
01:31:20,484 --> 01:31:24,484
Doesn't matter.
Either of its price is death.

756
01:31:24,484 --> 01:31:30,274
Master Yannis! Salvador saved our lives by
killing Edebali's dervishes.

757
01:31:30,274 --> 01:31:34,904
Princess is right.
We're alive thanks to Salvador.

758
01:31:35,540 --> 01:31:39,090
Plus, he was injured while
fighting beside us.

759
01:32:00,521 --> 01:32:06,591
Go to your room, son.
Wait for my word about your reward.

760
01:32:24,122 --> 01:32:26,372
Salvador is lying.

761
01:32:29,200 --> 01:32:30,320
But Master!

762
01:32:30,320 --> 01:32:33,480
One day, the rat in the church
make a decision after...

763
01:32:33,480 --> 01:32:37,840
... they are tired of
the cat bothering them.

764
01:32:38,173 --> 01:32:41,533
They will hang a bell to the cat's neck...

765
01:32:41,533 --> 01:32:45,533
... and they will know before he comes.

766
01:32:45,954 --> 01:32:50,394
So they will live peacefully.

767
01:32:50,544 --> 01:32:57,954
But they need a rat both brave and
stupid enough to hang the bell.

768
01:32:58,871 --> 01:33:03,491
Osman found that stupid rat.

769
01:33:06,882 --> 01:33:09,722
- Will you kill Salvador, Master?
- No.

770
01:33:10,476 --> 01:33:12,916
I will kill the cat.

771
01:33:13,563 --> 01:33:19,363
For that, I will use that stupid
and brave rat.

772
01:33:21,652 --> 01:33:23,592
How will you do that, Master?

773
01:33:28,737 --> 01:33:35,107
I will promote Salvador to
Commander of Kulucahisar?

774
01:33:52,084 --> 01:33:58,214
Balgay is calm for now.
But when he's available, he'll come at us.

775
01:34:00,303 --> 01:34:04,163
We need to increase
the Tent's safety measures.

776
01:34:04,163 --> 01:34:08,823
Thankfully, people trust us and
they have united once again.

777
01:34:09,052 --> 01:34:14,852
Now Balgay knows what is waiting for him.

778
01:34:15,098 --> 01:34:20,878
It's a good thing that Osman didn't kill
Dündar Bey after everything he did.

779
01:34:21,688 --> 01:34:25,198
Because establishing the unity you're
talking about would take time.

780
01:34:25,714 --> 01:34:28,094
Correct. Correct.

781
01:34:28,094 --> 01:34:31,964
- May I come in, Gündüz Bey?
- Come in, brother.

782
01:34:42,209 --> 01:34:43,879
Here, my brother.

783
01:34:54,100 --> 01:34:58,100
Brother. We need to find Balgay.

784
01:34:58,980 --> 01:35:03,300
He lost everything.
He probably will escape to Konya.

785
01:35:03,462 --> 01:35:07,262
If we don't prevent it,
he will come back more powerful than ever.

786
01:35:07,372 --> 01:35:10,652
What should we do?
What do you have in mind, Osman?

787
01:35:15,733 --> 01:35:21,123
If you allow it, I want to set off
with Konur and Boran.

788
01:35:21,123 --> 01:35:24,623
I will catch Balgay before
he goes to Konya.

789
01:35:24,967 --> 01:35:29,847
What if you can't catch him?
What if he arrives at Konya?

790
01:35:31,388 --> 01:35:34,758
Death doesn't care about
geography, Bamsı Bey.

791
01:35:35,393 --> 01:35:38,013
Then I will take his life in Konya.

792
01:35:38,165 --> 01:35:39,435
Nice.

793
01:35:42,179 --> 01:35:44,279
Keep an eye on the castle.

794
01:35:44,930 --> 01:35:48,590
Sıddık is still on duty.
He's waiting to hear from us.

795
01:35:48,891 --> 01:35:54,701
When the time comes, we'll fly the Kayı
flag on Kulucahisar, if Allah permits.

796
01:35:54,701 --> 01:35:59,571
Praise be! Don't look back, my valiant!

797
01:36:00,706 --> 01:36:02,346
Good luck!

798
01:36:03,348 --> 01:36:06,428
Thank you, Bamsı Bey.

799
01:36:07,616 --> 01:36:11,616
Before the funeral, Abdurrahman Gazi
will bring Dündar Bey to the Tent.

800
01:36:13,384 --> 01:36:19,324
He should say his last words to his son
with his wife before he is exiled.

801
01:36:20,254 --> 01:36:24,254
Brother. Don't tell anyone that
Dündar Bey is alive.

802
01:36:25,249 --> 01:36:28,859
I can only find out who played tricks on
us this way.

803
01:36:35,227 --> 01:36:36,637
Excuse me.

804
01:37:50,149 --> 01:37:54,469
We're going to a battle, Sıddık brother.
Osman Bey's orders.

805
01:37:54,776 --> 01:37:58,776
- Listen to me carefully.
- I'd die for Osman Bey's order!

806
01:37:59,217 --> 01:38:01,387
What do I need to do, Boran Alp?

807
01:38:02,712 --> 01:38:05,382
You will kidnap Sofia and
give her to Yannis.

808
01:38:05,382 --> 01:38:08,442
So they'll trust you more.

809
01:38:08,852 --> 01:38:13,032
When we arrive at the castle's gates
with flags of conquest...

810
01:38:13,467 --> 01:38:17,087
... you will be the one who
opens the castle's doors.

811
01:38:36,492 --> 01:38:41,752
Allah almighty, my duty is hard,
my burden is heavy.

812
01:38:42,426 --> 01:38:48,746
Don't let me be ashamed to Osman Bey,
and Osman Bey to Mohammad's people.

813
01:38:50,027 --> 01:38:58,407
Dear Allah, don't let Osman Bey and
his fellows be humiliated to infidels.

814
01:38:59,302 --> 01:39:04,702
Grant such a victory to them that
the oppressed be delighted.

815
01:39:07,073 --> 01:39:14,043
If you please, let Sıddık, this servant
of yours, be sacrificed.

816
01:39:15,586 --> 01:39:20,246
For the glory of İslam,
I'm willing to give up my spirit.

817
01:39:22,061 --> 01:39:26,211
As long as my life is sacrificed
for Muslims.

818
01:39:30,308 --> 01:39:37,258
You blessed me. In the end, allow me
to fall as a martyr, my Allah.

819
01:39:39,570 --> 01:39:40,520
Amen.

820
01:39:56,383 --> 01:39:59,683
Prince Salvador!
Master Yannis is waiting for you.

821
01:40:00,263 --> 01:40:01,803
I'm coming.

822
01:40:05,702 --> 01:40:09,432
Thousands of horseman will come after me.

823
01:40:10,334 --> 01:40:11,724
Just wait.

824
01:40:12,495 --> 01:40:14,735
Osman Bey will come.

825
01:40:43,245 --> 01:40:45,265
- Zorba.
- Yes, my Bey?

826
01:40:45,265 --> 01:40:48,465
Tell my soldiers to get
on with their duties.

827
01:40:49,047 --> 01:40:52,007
Gather those who are loyal to me.

828
01:40:52,391 --> 01:40:54,641
Tell them to come to the mansion tonight.

829
01:40:54,641 --> 01:40:58,601
Banner Lord Alişar Bey
will be having a great feast.

830
01:40:58,805 --> 01:41:00,305
As you wish, my Bey.

831
01:41:00,831 --> 01:41:01,651
Melik.

832
01:41:04,282 --> 01:41:10,702
Let the Tents know that I'm once again
the Banner Lord with the order of Geyhatu.

833
01:41:11,199 --> 01:41:13,049
If they refuse...

834
01:41:19,621 --> 01:41:22,261
... show them Geyhatu's commandment.

835
01:41:26,465 --> 01:41:30,465
- What if they resist?
- Make them worse than Balgay.

836
01:41:35,047 --> 01:41:40,057
They should know that I bashed Balgay's
head in. And they should act accordingly.

837
01:41:42,956 --> 01:41:45,166
And now for Kayıs...

838
01:41:46,915 --> 01:41:50,315
I will visit them myself.

839
01:41:51,902 --> 01:41:53,432
As you wish, my Bey.

840
01:42:09,168 --> 01:42:10,628
You made them steal my gold...

841
01:42:10,628 --> 01:42:14,058
... and made them come to the verge
of a battle with Kulucahisar.

842
01:42:14,058 --> 01:42:17,898
Is this how you protect the lands
I trusted you with?

843
01:42:19,278 --> 01:42:21,898
- Zorba.
- Yes, my Bey?

844
01:42:22,216 --> 01:42:24,216
Prepare my clothes.

845
01:42:26,102 --> 01:42:28,792
We're done with Balgay for now.

846
01:42:28,792 --> 01:42:32,432
Now I need to get even with
that woman called Sofia.

847
01:42:33,622 --> 01:42:37,242
- Did you put Dündar Bey in his room?
- I did, my Bey.

848
01:42:49,311 --> 01:42:55,951
I'm very happy. I told you. Your love is
different from those which fade away.

849
01:42:56,189 --> 01:42:58,819
I didn't want anything for myself
until today.

850
01:42:59,237 --> 01:43:03,607
If it's destiny, if we're
going to settle down with Osman...

851
01:43:04,675 --> 01:43:07,755
... my only wish will be to
give him a child, Gonca.

852
01:43:07,755 --> 01:43:10,675
If Allah permits, my Bala.

853
01:43:11,011 --> 01:43:13,811
That will happen too if Allah permits.

854
01:43:15,375 --> 01:43:17,035
May I come in?

855
01:43:19,166 --> 01:43:21,236
Come in, Osman Bey.

856
01:43:36,950 --> 01:43:39,230
I was about to go to Selcan Hatun.

857
01:43:40,395 --> 01:43:41,805
Excuse me.

858
01:43:59,131 --> 01:44:00,881
Now that I've seen that smile...

859
01:44:03,245 --> 01:44:06,765
Even if my path ends at the end
of the world, I won't worry.

860
01:44:08,830 --> 01:44:12,017
What path, Osman? What is it?

861
01:44:12,571 --> 01:44:14,801
I can't leave that Balgay dog alive.

862
01:44:15,366 --> 01:44:18,836
If I can't pursue him,
he will come back stronger.

863
01:44:19,996 --> 01:44:22,006
I hope the Mongol won't be big trouble.

864
01:44:22,156 --> 01:44:25,965
If I can't take Balgay's life,
this issue will grow bigger.

865
01:44:26,614 --> 01:44:31,934
If I catch him on the road, there, if not,
in Konya, I will kill him eventually.

866
01:44:33,825 --> 01:44:35,275
Don't leave the Tent...

867
01:44:36,366 --> 01:44:38,316
... if you don't have
to until I return.

868
01:44:38,589 --> 01:44:40,119
As you say.

869
01:44:40,614 --> 01:44:41,994
Don't worry about us.

870
01:44:42,784 --> 01:44:44,819
For the love of Allah, be careful.

871
01:44:46,999 --> 01:44:47,999
Oh...

872
01:44:49,839 --> 01:44:52,359
Are you afraid something
might happen to me?

873
01:44:52,919 --> 01:44:59,849
May Allah take your pain, ache,
troubles from you and give them to me.

874
01:44:59,857 --> 01:45:03,857
No. I wouldn't say "Amin"
to a prayer like that.

875
01:45:06,408 --> 01:45:07,688
If you are okay...

876
01:45:10,106 --> 01:45:11,546
... the rest is irrelevant.

877
01:45:16,795 --> 01:45:22,085
I don't know how, but when you smile,
I become much more powerful.

878
01:45:23,101 --> 01:45:26,541
I feel like I would crush the
mountains if they ask me to.

879
01:45:29,159 --> 01:45:34,309
Farewell, keep your love
and prayers with me.

880
01:45:36,117 --> 01:45:39,457
Both my prayers and my love is with you.

881
01:45:39,709 --> 01:45:41,539
May Allah watch over you.

882
01:46:13,329 --> 01:46:16,159
Dündar Bey, are you okay?

883
01:46:17,841 --> 01:46:22,841
I will host you in my mansion,
worthy of your pride, don't worry.

884
01:46:23,329 --> 01:46:27,329
Why did you- Why did you
bring me here, Alişar?

885
01:46:28,300 --> 01:46:32,300
I need to go to my Tent at once.

886
01:46:32,802 --> 01:46:36,802
Why, so that Osman can
finish what he started?

887
01:46:41,413 --> 01:46:47,293
Osman entered the Tent with Samsa's soldiers
and made Gündüz sit on his father's throne.

888
01:46:47,386 --> 01:46:51,996
- What?
- His brother will be a puppet for him.

889
01:46:52,974 --> 01:46:56,974
Until he becomes the Bey of the Tent.

890
01:46:58,663 --> 01:47:02,513
I own the Tent, Alişar Bey,
he can't do that.

891
01:47:03,274 --> 01:47:05,274
He told everyone that you died.

892
01:47:08,258 --> 01:47:14,788
Damn the day that I informed
Geyhatu and saved his life.

893
01:47:14,792 --> 01:47:17,472
I should've let Balgay take his life!

894
01:47:17,545 --> 01:47:20,385
Dündar Bey, Dündar Bey,
don't lose yourself.

895
01:47:22,910 --> 01:47:25,480
That was Osman's intentions
from the start.

896
01:47:26,681 --> 01:47:30,681
Then why didn't he kill me?

897
01:47:35,459 --> 01:47:38,679
Who knows what foul plans
does he have in his mind.

898
01:47:39,344 --> 01:47:45,414
Now, I will go and take Zöhre Hatun and
Aygül from the caged tent he put in.

899
01:47:46,523 --> 01:47:48,513
You should rest now.

900
01:47:49,941 --> 01:47:51,221
Zöhre.

901
01:47:54,016 --> 01:47:56,786
My daughter.

902
01:47:57,299 --> 01:48:00,559
Let them all know you as dead.

903
01:48:01,801 --> 01:48:07,491
Even if we can't know what they'll do to
Zöhre Hatun and Aygül if they find out.

904
01:48:08,861 --> 01:48:10,411
Isn't that right?

905
01:48:25,862 --> 01:48:27,092
My daughter.

906
01:48:28,504 --> 01:48:29,554
My daughter.

907
01:49:21,120 --> 01:49:26,810
Salvador, brave warrior of Catalonia.

908
01:49:27,414 --> 01:49:34,674
Rule with our Holy Father's justice,
and our Holy Mother's mercy.

909
01:49:38,172 --> 01:49:44,452
I declare you the
Commander of Kulucahisar!

910
01:49:51,617 --> 01:49:56,977
By the Father, Son and the Holy Spirit.

911
01:50:01,587 --> 01:50:07,767
If I stray away from our Holy Father's way
may this sword cut my flesh and bones.

912
01:50:20,822 --> 01:50:23,442
Alişar Bey is here, Princess,
he is waiting for you.

913
01:50:26,377 --> 01:50:28,057
Inform Master Yannis.

914
01:50:34,734 --> 01:50:35,814
Amen.

915
01:50:42,114 --> 01:50:51,074
I swear to be loyal to our Holy Father and
fight our enemies until my last breath!

916
01:50:51,090 --> 01:50:57,030
Commander Salvador!

917
01:50:57,503 --> 01:50:58,913
Alişar Bey is here, sir.

918
01:50:58,918 --> 01:51:09,468
Commander Salvador!

919
01:52:38,712 --> 01:52:42,782
I only got one question to
you, answer it correctly.

920
01:52:44,029 --> 01:52:47,279
What did Osman offer to
your father to betray Balgay?

921
01:52:51,293 --> 01:52:54,053
I am sure it wasn't
your miserable life.

922
01:52:54,732 --> 01:53:01,102
You know everything, I am sure
you know the answer to that too.

923
01:53:08,565 --> 01:53:11,955
Laws of Genghis Khan,
and the Dagger.

924
01:53:21,814 --> 01:53:22,774
And you...

925
01:53:25,666 --> 01:53:28,666
How could you be so brave to come here?

926
01:53:32,711 --> 01:53:37,621
Geyhatu ordered me to give this
letter to you as the Banner Lord.

927
01:54:02,492 --> 01:54:05,092
So, he wants the Laws and the Dagger.

928
01:54:08,615 --> 01:54:10,295
In exchange for what?

929
01:54:10,458 --> 01:54:15,248
Osman's death, and your life.

930
01:54:16,743 --> 01:54:19,993
Osman crushed Balgay himself.

931
01:54:21,492 --> 01:54:24,362
You know he'll be back for revenge.

932
01:54:26,614 --> 01:54:27,844
How could I...

933
01:54:29,848 --> 01:54:30,818
... trust Geyhatu...

934
01:54:32,257 --> 01:54:33,537
... or you?

935
01:54:44,772 --> 01:54:46,462
Your scent is killing me, Hatun.

936
01:54:49,432 --> 01:54:50,242
But...

937
01:54:51,830 --> 01:54:55,830
... you can't even imagine how bad
you'll smell when you're dead.

938
01:55:06,653 --> 01:55:09,193
I know the things you did behind me.

939
01:55:12,825 --> 01:55:17,745
I am ready to forget everything
if you are with me.

940
01:55:20,025 --> 01:55:25,335
We will both win if I kill
Osman and give Geyhatu...

941
01:55:27,836 --> 01:55:29,266
... Laws and the Dagger.

942
01:55:40,618 --> 01:55:43,368
Osman killed Dündar.

943
01:55:45,444 --> 01:55:47,844
He took the Tent with his brother.

944
01:55:50,085 --> 01:55:50,785
Now...

945
01:55:52,564 --> 01:55:53,684
... tell me...

946
01:55:56,824 --> 01:55:58,764
... what do you have in your hands?

947
01:56:02,152 --> 01:56:03,602
Dündar is alive...

948
01:56:05,362 --> 01:56:12,112
... only I can keep him, his stubborn
wife and his beautiful daughter alive.

949
01:56:14,050 --> 01:56:18,740
We will give Dündar his Tent back.
We will do this together.

950
01:56:24,940 --> 01:56:26,960
How can I trust Geyhatu?

951
01:56:27,328 --> 01:56:33,518
Geyhatu wants to marry Princess Adelfia to
improve trade relations with Byzantine.

952
01:56:34,468 --> 01:56:41,298
Princess is on her way to Konya.
Now we have one mutual enemy, Sofia.

953
01:56:42,244 --> 01:56:43,274
Osman.

954
01:56:49,803 --> 01:56:54,223
You are either with me,
or six feet under.

955
01:56:57,109 --> 01:56:58,129
Princess.

956
01:57:16,568 --> 01:57:22,088
Free me, Selcan Hatun, it's my right
to go to my brother's funeral.

957
01:57:22,954 --> 01:57:28,894
If this was about rights, my Batur
wouldn't deserve to die, Aygül.

958
01:57:38,370 --> 01:57:40,290
Listen carefully, Zöhre.

959
01:57:41,184 --> 01:57:45,184
You won't be able to live in
this Tent after what you did.

960
01:57:45,847 --> 01:57:50,507
Attend to your son's funeral,
then take your daughter and go.

961
01:57:52,123 --> 01:57:54,153
Go to the Mongols that you beg.

962
01:57:55,581 --> 01:57:57,301
What is the meaning of this?

963
01:57:59,839 --> 01:58:03,839
Punishment for treachery
is death in Oghuz Tradition.

964
01:58:05,262 --> 01:58:08,312
You should pray Gündüz Bey for his mercy.

965
01:58:13,009 --> 01:58:15,959
The ones who call us traitors
don't look to themselves.

966
01:58:16,977 --> 01:58:18,787
It's easy to call us traitors.

967
01:58:19,861 --> 01:58:20,891
Enough!

968
01:58:23,025 --> 01:58:25,715
You stubborn, shameless dog!

969
01:58:26,005 --> 01:58:28,765
This is all because of your greed!

970
01:58:28,859 --> 01:58:33,849
You couldn't stand to Osman, you even
went to Balgay and begged him!

971
01:58:34,040 --> 01:58:37,850
You lost your son but
still, you didn't stop. Enough!

972
01:58:37,882 --> 01:58:40,162
Selcan Hatun, stop.

973
01:58:41,764 --> 01:58:43,354
Free me.

974
01:59:03,757 --> 01:59:06,197
Go to your son and do your duty.

975
01:59:06,509 --> 01:59:11,739
Look at him, if you still have a
face to look, say your farewell. Hurry!

976
02:00:21,240 --> 02:00:25,590
You didn't disappoint us
with our faith in you, Osman Bey.

977
02:00:26,519 --> 02:00:28,469
You've repelled Balgay.

978
02:00:28,765 --> 02:00:32,105
War is ours, victory is Allah's.

979
02:00:33,170 --> 02:00:39,650
Thank Allah, now Balgay has seen that the
Turks will never surrender to anyone too.

980
02:00:41,056 --> 02:00:46,736
But it will get harder
from now on, know that.

981
02:00:48,399 --> 02:00:53,339
If I don't destroy Balgay, he will
come back with a bigger force.

982
02:00:54,126 --> 02:00:56,826
Our issue is bigger than that.

983
02:00:57,862 --> 02:01:01,422
Now, our fight will be even harsher.

984
02:01:02,109 --> 02:01:06,109
Now, listen to me carefully, son.

985
02:01:09,506 --> 02:01:16,006
While we are making moves, the
devil's army attacks without stopping.

986
02:01:17,119 --> 02:01:21,379
Geyhatu has declared Alişar
as the banner lord again.

987
02:01:21,570 --> 02:01:24,980
Because he is not in
good terms with Balgay.

988
02:01:25,565 --> 02:01:30,685
Because of Genghis Khan's Laws,
Balgay disappointed Geyhatu.

989
02:01:31,812 --> 02:01:38,092
It's clear that he will come back and
haunt the Turkish Tents with this rage.

990
02:01:38,563 --> 02:01:40,603
We've finished Balgay's courage.

991
02:01:41,576 --> 02:01:44,606
Now he is in no place to spread fear.

992
02:01:45,158 --> 02:01:49,758
We will fight him with everything we got.
We will continue to do so.

993
02:01:50,214 --> 02:01:53,914
Thank you, there is
no doubt about that.

994
02:01:54,478 --> 02:02:00,128
Now we have more important
business with Balgay.

995
02:02:01,627 --> 02:02:06,177
Princess Adelfa, who
lives in Constantinopolis...

996
02:02:06,536 --> 02:02:12,546
... will be married to the Mongolian
governor Geyhatu by the Emperor.

997
02:02:14,981 --> 02:02:16,101
That means...

998
02:02:17,889 --> 02:02:20,349
... a Mongolian-Byzantine alliance.

999
02:02:20,773 --> 02:02:25,483
Alliance for them,
doomsday for the Turks.

1000
02:02:28,504 --> 02:02:33,394
The Tents in the edges will
be caught in the crossfire.

1001
02:02:34,143 --> 02:02:40,663
Osman Bey, you need to prevent
this marriage from happening.

1002
02:02:41,564 --> 02:02:45,144
Princess Adelfa doesn't
want this marriage.

1003
02:02:45,798 --> 02:02:52,738
But what's important is taking Princess
